This study was approved by the research ethics committee of the First Affiliated Hospital of Zhengzhou University (2018-KY-88). A total of 496 patients with psychiatric disorders and 255 heathy controls from three independent datasets (one discovery dataset and two validation datasets) were included in this study. Additionally, another extensive dataset comprising 492 healthy individuals aged 19 -80 was included to construct a normal structural covariance network (see Methods). The discovery dataset was obtained from the University of California, Los Angeles (UCLA) Consortium for Neuropsychiatric Phenomics (CNP) and is available on the public database OpenfMRI (Poldrack et al., 2016).

Fig. 1. The workflow of this study. For each brain region, individualized gray matter volume/morphological (GMV) abnormalities are obtained using normative modeling and used to identify transdiagnostic subtypes. A series of sensitivity analyses are conducted to assess the reproducibility and generalizability of clustering outcomes. To gain deeper insights into the subtypes, we investigate their disease epicenters, and molecular and genetic underpinnings.

![Image](./Fang2024_artifacts/image_000007_b29363b7f044e0df0a14da99b241b54048b875aa125152bbb952470868bbf1b2.png)

K. Fang et al.

The CNP dataset, approved by the Institutional Review Boards at UCLA and  the  Los  Angeles  County  Department  of  Mental  Health,  includes multimodal  imaging  from  142  patients  with  psychiatric  disorders, including schizophrenia ( n = 50), bipolar disorder (BD, n = 49), and attention  deficit  hyperactivity  disorder  (ADHD, n = 43),  as  well  as healthy controls (HCs, n = 130). Diagnoses were based on the Structured Clinical Interview for DSM-IV-Text Revision (Poldrack et al., 2016). The validation  dataset  1  was  obtained  from  the  Centre  for  Biomedical Research  Excellence  (COBRE)  and  is  available  at  http://fcon\_1000. projects.nitrc.org/indi/retro/cobre.html (Collin et al., 2014). The COBRE group comprised 72 patients with schizophrenia and matched 74 HCs. The validation dataset 2 was obtained from site 20 of the Depression Imaging Research Consortium (DIRECT) (Chen et al., 2022; Yan et al., 2019). The single-site dataset with the largest sample size (site 20) was  used  to  prevent  multi-site  effects  on  the  results.  This  dataset comprised data from 282 patients with depression and 251 matched HCs. All study procedures were in accordance with the Declaration of Helsinki of 1975 and approved by the local Research Ethics Committees. More  details  regarding  the  datasets,  data  acquisition,  and  data  preprocessing are described in the Supplementary Methods.

## 2.2. Subtyping analysis based on individualized gray matter morphological abnormalities


